<newsitem itemid="89501" id="root" date="1996-10-01" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Frogmore year pre-tax profits rises.</title>
<headline>Frogmore year pre-tax profits rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr, basic (pence)	     18.0	  vs 22.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)		 14.9	  vs 14.0</p>
<p> Total Dividend (pence)	 19.0	  vs 18.0</p>
<p> Pretax			     15.55	 vs 14.90</p>
<p> Turnover			   147.27	vs 72.40</p>
<p> Operating result		 28.76	 vs 21.01</p>
<p> Net asset value(pence)	 454	   vs 473</p>
<p> Pay date		   Nov 25</p>
<p>Div  registration date Nov 5 Note - Frogmore Estates Plc, a property investment, development and trading company, net borrowings fell to 114.3 million stg from 120.8 million representing gearing of 49 percent.</p>
<p>Frogmore said this level of gearing and the undrawn committed facilities available to the company provide ample scope for further acquisitions.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
